      "content": "Transitioning to a decentralized model with 50 regional nodes would likely fragment your visibility and control, potentially causing initial dips in global fulfillment rates as systems stabilize. While this approach mitigates single-point-of-failure risks, the complexity of managing 50 distinct regions could introduce logistical friction that slows order processing speed. Weighing the resilience benefits against the operational overhead, I recommend a hybrid model where core global orchestration is retained but operates alongside key regional hubs to maintain consistency. Would you like me to draft a comparison matrix outlining the trade-offs between centralized and decentralized execution timelines?",
